{
  "summary": "Sanitizes error messages across descriptor parsing, wallet imports, and transaction funding to avoid reflecting raw input strings or key material. Error paths replace quoted input text with positional key indices or public descriptor representations (`desc->ToString()`), remove echoed invalid characters and checksums, and restrict quoted function names to an allowlist of recognized descriptor and Miniscript keywords.",
  "problem": "Descriptors can contain sensitive private keys such as WIF strings or xprvs. When parsing or derivation fails—often due to syntax errors, stray delimiters, or derivation issues—the resulting error strings quote the raw inputs, exposing secret key material in RPC error responses, application logs, monitoring services, or shared screenshots.",
  "evidence": [
    "Commit message notes that 'Error text is often logged or shared where the request is not. Even the first characters of a key give away part of it.'",
    "Test changes demonstrate that syntax errors with invalid characters previously leaked WIF keys and xprv substrings into RPC exception messages."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "Modifies error strings across the descriptor parser, BIP32 keypath parsing, and wallet RPCs, requiring updates to numerous functional and unit test assertions that match on exact error text.",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "Stops descriptor parsing, wallet imports, and transaction funding errors from echoing raw key material. Descriptors can contain private keys, and syntax or derivation errors previously reflected raw input fragments or full descriptors into error responses, risking exposure in application logs or shared screenshots. The change replaces echoed inputs with positional indices or public descriptor representations, omits malformed text from error strings, and restricts function name quoting to a static allowlist. New and updated tests verify that private key substrings do not leak into error messages.",
  "needs": [],
  "confidence": "high",
  "uncertainties": [],
  "risk": {
    "level": "medium",
    "touches": ["wallet", "rpc_api"],
    "why": "Modifying RPC error strings can break downstream tooling or external applications that match on exact error text."
  }
}
